# the name is computed, not only `send` and `public_send`: `__send__`, `try`
# and `method` once came out clear. A literal name lowers the method it
# names, not its file, and says so beside a call too (Stringed, Inlined,
# Labeled, whose `named:` once hid the string; Called, a symbol). A send
# behind a literal send of a send is read (Meta, Restrung). Any string's
# text that spells a send lowers its file: code strings read by a parse
# came out clear when an interpolation spelled the name (Spelled, Holed,
# Nested), when the code was escaped (Escaped) or built (Joined), or on a
# receiver extraction does not read (Tracking); so does one without
# parentheses (Unbracketed; `send n` is English as often, so Bare is
# unread), and code after `__END__` (Trailing). A
# name sent that is an alias names its target (Aliased); `send(:method, x)`
# runs nothing (Handle).
